cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Tropical Resource Typing"
abstract: "Lean 4 applied to max-plus (tropical) algebra to resource-aware type systems for compositional worst-case bounds. Provides a reusable resource-grade axis with parametric transport, a no-go theorem (hub_ceiling) refuting Protocol Squisher's universal-interoperability claim; separation proofs distinguishing tropical instances from finite {0,1,ω} reifications; and a separation proof that resource algebras measure Echo residues but are not Echo instances."
authors:
